<title>SWEDEN: Sydkraft posts largely unchanged 1996 profit.</title>
<headline>Sydkraft posts largely unchanged 1996 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish power company Sydkraft</p>
<p>AB presented these earnings for 1996 on Thursday.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		2,504 vs  2,499</p>
<p> Turnover				 13,572 vs 12,155</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (crowns)	   4.00 vs   3.75</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	  9.52 vs   9.37</p>
<p> Operating costs			 8,951 vs  7,413</p>
<p> Depreciation			    1,278 vs  1,257</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec     3,343 vs  3,485</p>
<p> Financial income			  264 vs    318</p>
<p> Associated interest		     117 vs     58</p>
<p> Financial costs			 1,220 vs  1,362</p>
<p> Minorities		     CHARGE    16 vs     20  CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					   670 vs    689</p>
<p> Net profit				1,818 vs  1,790</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll of eight analysts showed expectations for a profit after financial items of 2.45 billion crowns. The company itself has said it expected a profit of 2.4 billion crowns after financial items for the year.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
